      "id": 136757,
      "name": "MarioFanaticXV",
      "username": "MarioFanaticXV",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mariofanaticxv/{size}/2129_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-03-05T19:41:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Being able to hit \"Enter\" for \"Yes\" seems pretty standard, but enter has no function as far as I can tell. Also, it feels odd that I can't use the arrow keys to scroll. They could also imlement other keyboard shortcuts pretty easily; such as Backspace for the rewind feature (or Ctrl+Z since that's often asigned to Undo), and maybe something for the \"check powers\" button. Or even just bindable keys.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>And an interface that allows one to use a gamepad would be a nice option as well- it's just the fact that it's 5 USD more than the tablet version yet feels exactly like it would if I bought the tablet version and used an android emulator to play it that bothers me- if it's going to be more expensive, it should have more features, especially since the development costs for the PC are definitely cheaper than they are for iOS with all of Apple's bureaucracy (can't speak about how it compares to Android, not sure about that one, I know that also beats out iOS though).</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:13:00.510Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
