      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>Being able to hit &quot;Enter&quot; for &quot;Yes&quot; seems pretty standard, but enter has no function as far as I can tell. Also, it feels odd that I can&#39;t use the arrow keys to scroll. They could also imlement other keyboard shortcuts pretty easily; such as Backspace for the rewind feature (or Ctrl+Z since that&#39;s often asigned to Undo), and maybe something for the &quot;check powers&quot; button. Or even just bindable keys.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>And an interface that allows one to use a gamepad would be a nice option as well- it&#39;s just the fact that it&#39;s 5 USD more than the tablet version yet feels exactly like it would if I bought the tablet version and used an android emulator to play it that bothers me- if it&#39;s going to be more expensive, it should have more features, especially since the development costs for the PC are definitely cheaper than they are for iOS with all of Apple&#39;s bureaucracy (can&#39;t speak about how it compares to Android, not sure about that one, I know that also beats out iOS though).</p>",
