      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "[quote=\"MarioFanaticXV\"]\n\n... it&#39;s just the fact that it&#39;s 5 USD more than the tablet version ...- if it&#39;s going to be more expensive, it should have more features ...\n\n[/quote]\n\nThis is my intuition, too, but ... I wonder.&nbsp; How does one price these things?&nbsp; \n\n&nbsp;\n\nDespite my sense that the same game &quot;should&quot; cost the same on different platforms, I have disparate impressions of how much games on different platforms &quot;should&quot; cost: My intuitiion for PC is that $15 is relatively INexpensive, but my intuition for an iOS or Android app is that $10 is pretty expensive.&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n Economics suggests that the best price is the one on the demand curve that maximizes profit, and maybe that&#39;s what is going on here. They&#39;ve priced the game differently on different platforms because the demand curves on those platforms are different. \n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n",
